# Copy to .env and fill in. Discord Developer Portal → your application
# (https://discord.com/developers/applications). Never commit .env.
#
# .env is read in two places on your machine:
#   - `pnpm deploy-commands` uses DISCORD_TOKEN and DISCORD_CLIENT_ID to register slash commands.
#   - `pnpm dev` (wrangler dev) passes these to the local Worker, which uses DISCORD_PUBLIC_KEY to
#     verify interactions and DISCORD_TOKEN for the Gateway connection (inline verses).
# The deployed Worker doesn't read .env: set its secrets with `pnpm wrangler secret put DISCORD_PUBLIC_KEY`
# and `pnpm wrangler secret put DISCORD_TOKEN`.
# Don't create a .dev.vars file: if one exists, wrangler dev reads it instead of .env.
# For local development, use a separate Discord application's values, so your local copy doesn't
# share a bot (and double every reply) with the deployed one.

# Bot → Token
DISCORD_TOKEN=your-bot-token
# General Information → Application ID
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=your-application-id
# General Information → Public Key
DISCORD_PUBLIC_KEY=your-public-key
